<title>CANADA: TABLE - Canada M1 money supply rises in June.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Canada M1 money supply rises in June.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian M1 money supply rose by C$1.64 billion to C$72.65 billion in June from C$71.01 billion in May, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>					   June 97     May 97    June 96</p>
<p>M1					  72.65	71.01	62.82</p>
<p>M2					 393.73     391.81     392.49</p>
<p>M3					 507.26     505.67     482.38</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets			 June	  May</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-16.72	-14.59</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     726.72	714.36</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    105.65	102.60</p>
<p>				    Wk to Jul 16  Chg on wk  Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  28.136  -0.237     +1.116</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     6.898  +0.735     +0.049</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	457.647  +1.332     -5.566</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 122.800   0.000    -30.800</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  32.194  -0.029     +1.928</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
</text>
